 "standard_text": "Use the following rules of differentiation: d/dx[xⁿ] = nxⁿ⁻¹; d/dx[k f(x)] = k d/dx[f(x)]; d/dx[f(x) ± g(x)] = d/dx[f(x)] ± d/dx[g(x)].",
 "meta_desc": "Free CAPS Grade 12 calculus worksheets: the power rule, polynomials, negative and fractional exponents and simplifying before differentiating. 100 questions with memos.",
 "key_big": "d/dx(axⁿ) = naxⁿ⁻¹.",
 "key_sub": "Write roots and fractions as powers first.",
 "body_html": "<h2>How to think about it</h2><ul><li>Power rule: <span class='fr'><span class='fn'>d</span><span class='fd'>dx</span></span>(axⁿ) = naxⁿ⁻¹.</li><li>The derivative of a constant is 0; differentiate a sum term by term.</li><li>Write roots and fractions as powers first: √x = x<sup>½</sup>, <span class='fr'><span class='fn'>1</span><span class='fd'>x²</span></span> = x<sup>−2</sup>.</li><li>Expand brackets or divide by x before you differentiate.</li></ul><h2>Examples</h2><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>y = 4x³ − 2x + 7</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>12x² − 2 + 0</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: dy/dx = 12x² − 2</p></div><h2>Common mistakes</h2><div class='sn-tw'><table class='sn-table'><thead><tr><th>Mistake</th><th>What to do instead</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>The power</td><td>Subtract 1 from the power.</td></tr><tr><td>Constants</td><td>d/dx(7) = 0.</td></tr><tr><td>Products</td><td>Expand first: (x + 1)(x − 2) = x² − x − 2.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>",
 "faq": [
